{
 "format": "velophi-apparatus",
 "version": 1,
 "note": "What each piece of apparatus IS to the bench (26.64, D269; 26.65, D297: role support — a stand, a tripod, a rack — and the burners, the hot plate and the baths are things of their own on the bench, drawing only, kept in the document's fixtures; where they stand decides the heat and bath actions of the log). role vessel: an object of the core (capacity, heat capacity of the glass = glass_g x cp_J_gK, heat loss to the room loss_W_K at the reference capacity, scaled with capacity^(2/3)); role instrument: reads one field of the vessel it is put in, to its resolution; role tool: performs one action of the log on the vessel it is on. available false: the function is not in the core yet (reason) - such a kind is in the data and not on the shelf. Profiles: inner radius r (cm) against height h (cm) at the reference capacity ref_mL, from the bottom; the drawing and the liquid level both use them, scaled so that the volume up to `full` is exactly the capacity. Glass masses are typical values of school borosilicate ware (to about 20 %); cp 0.84 J/(g K) borosilicate glass, 1.05 porcelain, 1.3 expanded polystyrene. Burner powers are the heat that reaches the vessel, order of magnitude. Litmus changes colour between pH 4.5 and 8.3. The spectrophotometer reads the absorbance of a 1 cm cuvette at the wavelength of the strongest absorption among the sixteen of the core. Cobalt glass absorbs the yellow sodium lines.",
